-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 6, Chapter 2 (EARNED INCOME): regulations 51 to 56, 60 and 61.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (lines 877-969 and 1028-1056), a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text. Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Money is a NUMBER of pounds; a calculated amount is rounded once, at the end, with
-- the keel's `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (regulation 6(1)). Self-employed earnings (regulations 57 to 59) are
-- in uc2-part6-ch2-self-employed.l4; surplus earnings (54A), the minimum income floor and gainful self-employment (62 to 64)
-- are in uc2-part6-ch2-surplus-and-floor.l4.

§ `Part 6, Chapter 2 -- Earned income`

§§ `Chapter heading and regulation 51 -- Introduction (inert)`
-- src:877 | CHAPTER 2 — EARNED INCOME
-- src:878 | 51 Introduction
-- src:879 | This Chapter provides for the calculation or estimation of a person's earned income for the purposes of section 8 of the Act (calculation of awards).
-- INERT: the Chapter heading and a statement of what the Chapter is for. It cites section 8 of the Act (calculation of awards),
-- which is not an input, and decides nothing a person could ask.

§§ `Regulation 52 -- Meaning of "earned income"`

-- src:880 | 52 Meaning of “earned income”
-- src:881 | “Earned income” means—
-- src:882 | (a) the remuneration or profits derived from—
-- src:883 | (i) employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office,
-- src:884 | (ii) a trade, profession or vocation, or
-- src:885 | (iii) any other paid work; or
-- src:886 | (b) any income treated as earned income in accordance with this Chapter.
@ref reg 52 (src:880-886)
DECLARE `Income considered under regulation 52` HAS
    `remuneration or profits derived from employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `remuneration or profits derived from a trade, profession or vocation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `income derived from work done by the person`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `work from which the income is derived`                                 IS A `Work done by a person`
    `income treated as earned income in accordance with this Chapter`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:882 | (a) the remuneration or profits derived from—
-- src:883 | (i) employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office,
-- src:884 | (ii) a trade, profession or vocation, or
-- src:885 | (iii) any other paid work; or
@ref reg 52(a) (src:882-885)
GIVEN income IS AN `Income considered under regulation 52`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 52(a)(iii) — remuneration or profits derived from any other paid work` income MEANS
        (income's `income derived from work done by the person`)
    AND (`reg 2 — paid work` (income's `work from which the income is derived`))

-- src:882 | (a) the remuneration or profits derived from—
-- src:883 | (i) employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office,
-- src:884 | (ii) a trade, profession or vocation, or
-- src:885 | (iii) any other paid work; or
@ref reg 52(a) (src:882-885)
GIVEN income IS AN `Income considered under regulation 52`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 52(a) — remuneration or profits` income MEANS
        (income's `remuneration or profits derived from employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office`)
    OR  (income's `remuneration or profits derived from a trade, profession or vocation`)
    OR  (`reg 52(a)(iii) — remuneration or profits derived from any other paid work` income)

-- src:880 | 52 Meaning of “earned income”
-- src:881 | “Earned income” means—
-- src:882 | (a) the remuneration or profits derived from—
-- src:883 | (i) employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office,
-- src:884 | (ii) a trade, profession or vocation, or
-- src:885 | (iii) any other paid work; or
-- src:886 | (b) any income treated as earned income in accordance with this Chapter.
@ref reg 52 (src:880-886)
GIVEN income IS AN `Income considered under regulation 52`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 52 — income is earned income` income MEANS
        (`reg 52(a) — remuneration or profits` income)
    OR  (income's `income treated as earned income in accordance with this Chapter`)

§§ `Regulation 53(1) -- Definitions (inert: cross-references and citations)`
-- src:887 | 53 Meaning of other terms relating to earned income
-- src:888 | (1) In this Chapter—
-- src:889 | “car” has the meaning in section 268A of the Capital Allowances Act 2001 ;
-- src:890 | “employed earnings” has the meaning in regulation 55;
-- src:891 | “gainful self-employment” has the meaning in regulation 64;
-- src:892 | “HMRC” means Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs;
-- src:893 | “motor cycle” has the meaning in section 268A of the Capital Allowances Act 2001;
-- src:894 | “ PAYE Regulations” means the Income Tax (Pay As You Earn) Regulations 2003 ;
-- src:895 | “relievable pension contributions” has the meaning in section 188 of the Finance Act 2004 ;
-- src:896 | “self-employed earnings” has the meaning in regulation 57; and
-- src:897 | “start-up period” has the meaning in regulation 63.
-- INERT as a rule: the definitions in paragraph (1) either point to another regulation of this Chapter ("employed earnings" 55,
-- "gainful self-employment" 64, "self-employed earnings" 57, "start-up period" 63), or define a term by pure citation of an Act or
-- of regulations that are not inputs ("car" and "motor cycle" in section 268A of the Capital Allowances Act 2001; "HMRC";
-- "PAYE Regulations"; "relievable pension contributions" in section 188 of the Finance Act 2004). Each cited term is a stated
-- input where a rule needs it: a NUMBER of relievable pension contributions, a BOOLEAN for whether a vehicle is a car.

§§ `Regulation 53(2) -- Participating as a service user`

-- src:898 | (2) References in this Chapter to a person participating as a service user are to—
-- src:899 | (a) a person who is being consulted by or on behalf of—
-- src:900 | (i) a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing; or
-- src:901 | (ii) a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services,
-- src:902 | in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services; or
-- src:903 | (ab) a person who is being consulted by or on behalf of—
-- src:904 | (i) the Secretary of State in relation to any of the Secretary of State’s functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973; or
-- src:905 | (ii) a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions,
-- src:906 | in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person;
-- src:907 | (b) the carer of a person consulted under sub-paragraphs (a) or (ab).
@ref reg 53(2) (src:898-907)
DECLARE `Person who may be participating as a service user` HAS
    `consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `consulted in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `consulted in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the carer of a person consulted under sub-paragraph (a) or (ab)`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:899 | (a) a person who is being consulted by or on behalf of—
-- src:900 | (i) a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing; or
-- src:901 | (ii) a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services,
-- src:902 | in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services; or
@ref reg 53(2)(a) (src:899-902)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 53(2)(a) — the body consulting about services` person MEANS
        (person's `consulted by or on behalf of a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing`)
    OR  (person's `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services`)

-- src:899 | (a) a person who is being consulted by or on behalf of—
-- src:900 | (i) a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing; or
-- src:901 | (ii) a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services,
-- src:902 | in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services; or
@ref reg 53(2)(a) (src:899-902)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 53(2)(a) — consulted about services` person MEANS
        (`reg 53(2)(a) — the body consulting about services` person)
    AND (person's `consulted in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services`)

-- src:903 | (ab) a person who is being consulted by or on behalf of—
-- src:904 | (i) the Secretary of State in relation to any of the Secretary of State’s functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973; or
-- src:905 | (ii) a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions,
-- src:906 | in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person;
@ref reg 53(2)(ab) (src:903-906)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 53(2)(ab) — the body consulting about functions` person MEANS
        (person's `consulted by or on behalf of the Secretary of State in relation to the Secretary of State's functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973`)
    OR  (person's `consulted by or on behalf of a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions`)

-- src:903 | (ab) a person who is being consulted by or on behalf of—
-- src:904 | (i) the Secretary of State in relation to any of the Secretary of State’s functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973; or
-- src:905 | (ii) a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions,
-- src:906 | in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person;
@ref reg 53(2)(ab) (src:903-906)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 53(2)(ab) — consulted about functions` person MEANS
        (`reg 53(2)(ab) — the body consulting about functions` person)
    AND (person's `consulted in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person`)

-- src:898 | (2) References in this Chapter to a person participating as a service user are to—
-- src:899 | (a) a person who is being consulted by or on behalf of—
-- src:900 | (i) a body which has a statutory duty to provide services in the field of health, social care or social housing; or
-- src:901 | (ii) a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such services,
-- src:902 | in their capacity as a user, potential user, carer of a user or person otherwise affected by the provision of those services; or
-- src:903 | (ab) a person who is being consulted by or on behalf of—
-- src:904 | (i) the Secretary of State in relation to any of the Secretary of State’s functions in the field of social security or child support or under section 2 of the Employment and Training Act 1973; or
-- src:905 | (ii) a body which conducts research or undertakes monitoring for the purpose of planning or improving such functions,
-- src:906 | in their capacity as a person affected or potentially affected by the exercise of those functions or the carer of such a person;
-- src:907 | (b) the carer of a person consulted under sub-paragraphs (a) or (ab).
@ref reg 53(2) (src:898-907)
GIVEN person IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` person MEANS
        (`reg 53(2)(a) — consulted about services` person)
    OR  (`reg 53(2)(ab) — consulted about functions` person)
    OR  (person's `the carer of a person consulted under sub-paragraph (a) or (ab)`)

§§ `Regulation 54 -- Calculation of earned income: general principles`

-- Paragraph (2): in two cases the Secretary of State's determination may be based on an estimate of the amounts received or
-- expected to be received in the assessment period. Whether an estimate is in fact made is the Secretary of State's choice.
-- src:910 | (2) Where the Secretary of State—
-- src:911 | (a) makes a determination as to whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim for universal credit; or
-- src:912 | (b) makes a determination as to the amount of a person's earned income in relation to an assessment period where a person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income,
-- src:913 | that determination may be based on an estimate of the amounts received or expected to be received in that assessment period.
@ref reg 54(2) (src:910-913)
DECLARE `Determination that may be based on an estimate` HAS
    `determination of whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met, made before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `determination of the amount of the person's earned income for an assessment period, where the person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:910 | (2) Where the Secretary of State—
-- src:911 | (a) makes a determination as to whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim for universal credit; or
-- src:912 | (b) makes a determination as to the amount of a person's earned income in relation to an assessment period where a person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income,
-- src:913 | that determination may be based on an estimate of the amounts received or expected to be received in that assessment period.
@ref reg 54(2) (src:910-913)
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination that may be based on an estimate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 54(2) — the determination may be based on an estimate` determination MEANS
        (determination's `determination of whether the financial conditions in section 5 of the Act are met, made before the expiry of the first assessment period in relation to a claim`)
    OR  (determination's `determination of the amount of the person's earned income for an assessment period, where the person has failed to report information in relation to that earned income`)

-- Paragraph (1): unless otherwise provided in the Chapter, the actual amounts received in the period. Where paragraph (2) lets the
-- determination rest on an estimate and the Secretary of State has made one, the estimate stands in place of the actual amounts.
-- src:908 | 54 Calculation of earned income - general principles
-- src:909 | (1) The calculation of a person's earned income in respect of an assessment period is, unless otherwise provided in this Chapter, to be based on the actual amounts received in that period.
@ref reg 54(1) (src:908-909)
GIVEN determination IS A `Determination that may be based on an estimate`
      `actual amounts received in the assessment period` IS A NUMBER
      `estimate of the amounts received or expected to be received in the assessment period made by the Secretary of State` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 54(1) — the amounts on which the earned income for an assessment period is based` determination `actual amounts received in the assessment period` `estimate of the amounts received or expected to be received in the assessment period made by the Secretary of State` MEANS
    IF `reg 54(2) — the determination may be based on an estimate` determination
    THEN (CONSIDER `estimate of the amounts received or expected to be received in the assessment period made by the Secretary of State`
          WHEN JUST estimate THEN estimate
          WHEN NOTHING THEN `actual amounts received in the assessment period`)
    ELSE `actual amounts received in the assessment period`

§§ `Regulation 55 -- Employed earnings`

§§ `Regulation 55(1) -- Scope (inert)`
-- src:946 | 55 Employed earnings
-- src:947 | (1) This regulation applies for the purposes of calculating earned income from employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office (“employed earnings”).
-- INERT: paragraph (1) says what the regulation is for ("calculating earned income from employment under a contract of service or
-- in an office, including elective office"). The rules below are called for that income and for no other.

§§ `Regulation 55(2) to (5) -- What employed earnings are`

-- src:954 | (4) The following benefits are to be treated as employed earnings—
-- src:955 | (a) statutory sick pay;
-- src:956 | (b) statutory maternity pay;
-- src:957 | (c) ... statutory paternity pay;
-- src:958 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:959 | (e) statutory adoption pay; ...
-- src:960 | (f) statutory shared parental pay; ...
-- src:961 | (g) statutory parental bereavement pay ; and
-- src:962 | (h) statutory neonatal care pay.
@ref reg 55(4) (src:954-962)
DECLARE `Payment of a benefit` HAS
    benefit  IS A Benefit
    amount   IS A NUMBER

-- src:946 | 55 Employed earnings
-- src:947 | (1) This regulation applies for the purposes of calculating earned income from employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office (“employed earnings”).
-- src:948 | (2) Employed earnings comprise any amounts that are general earnings, as defined in section 7(3) of ITEPA, but excluding—
-- src:949 | (a) amounts that are treated as earnings under Chapters 2 to 11 of Part 3 of ITEPA (the benefits code); and
-- src:950 | (b) amounts that are exempt from income tax under Part 4 of ITEPA.
-- src:951 | (3) In the calculation of employed earnings the following are to be disregarded—
-- src:952 | (a) expenses that are allowed to be deducted under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA; and
-- src:953 | (b) expenses arising from participation as a service user (see regulation 53(2)).
-- src:954 | (4) The following benefits are to be treated as employed earnings—
-- src:955 | (a) statutory sick pay;
-- src:956 | (b) statutory maternity pay;
-- src:957 | (c) ... statutory paternity pay;
-- src:958 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:959 | (e) statutory adoption pay; ...
-- src:960 | (f) statutory shared parental pay; ...
-- src:961 | (g) statutory parental bereavement pay ; and
-- src:962 | (h) statutory neonatal care pay.
-- src:963 | (4A) A repayment of income tax or national insurance contributions received by a person from HMRC in respect of a tax year in which the person was in paid work is to be treated as employed earnings unless it is taken into account as self-employed earnings under regulation 57(4).
-- src:964 | (5) In calculating the amount of a person's employed earnings in respect of an assessment period, there are to be deducted from the amount of general earnings or benefits specified in paragraphs (2) to (4)—
-- src:965 | (a) any relievable pension contributions made by the person in that period;
-- src:966 | (b) any amounts paid by the person in that period in respect of the employment by way of income tax or primary Class 1 contributions under section 6(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act; and
-- src:967 | (c) any sums withheld as donations to an approved scheme under Part 12 of ITEPA (payroll giving) by a person required to make deductions or repayments of income tax under the PAYE Regulations.
@ref reg 55 (src:946-967)
DECLARE `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period` HAS
    `general earnings as defined in section 7(3) of ITEPA`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `of which amounts treated as earnings under Chapters 2 to 11 of Part 3 of ITEPA (the benefits code)`  IS A NUMBER
    `of which amounts exempt from income tax under Part 4 of ITEPA`                              IS A NUMBER
    `of which expenses allowed to be deducted under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA`                IS A NUMBER
    `of which expenses arising from participation as a service user`                             IS A NUMBER
    `service user participation of the person`                                                   IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
    `benefits received`                                                                           IS A LIST OF `Payment of a benefit`
    `repayment of income tax or national insurance contributions received from HMRC in respect of a tax year`  IS A NUMBER
    `work done by the person in that tax year`                                                   IS A `Work done by a person`
    `the repayment is taken into account as self-employed earnings under regulation 57(4)`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period`              IS A NUMBER
    `amounts paid by the person in the assessment period in respect of the employment by way of income tax or primary Class 1 contributions`  IS A NUMBER
    `sums withheld as donations to an approved scheme under Part 12 of ITEPA (payroll giving)`   IS A NUMBER

-- src:948 | (2) Employed earnings comprise any amounts that are general earnings, as defined in section 7(3) of ITEPA, but excluding—
-- src:949 | (a) amounts that are treated as earnings under Chapters 2 to 11 of Part 3 of ITEPA (the benefits code); and
-- src:950 | (b) amounts that are exempt from income tax under Part 4 of ITEPA.
@ref reg 55(2) (src:948-950)
GIVEN amounts IS AN `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 55(2) — the general earnings that comprise employed earnings` amounts MEANS
        (amounts's `general earnings as defined in section 7(3) of ITEPA`)
    MINUS (amounts's `of which amounts treated as earnings under Chapters 2 to 11 of Part 3 of ITEPA (the benefits code)`)
    MINUS (amounts's `of which amounts exempt from income tax under Part 4 of ITEPA`)

-- src:951 | (3) In the calculation of employed earnings the following are to be disregarded—
-- src:952 | (a) expenses that are allowed to be deducted under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA; and
-- src:953 | (b) expenses arising from participation as a service user (see regulation 53(2)).
@ref reg 55(3) (src:951-953)
GIVEN amounts IS AN `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 55(3) — the amounts disregarded` amounts MEANS
        (amounts's `of which expenses allowed to be deducted under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA`)
    PLUS (IF `reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (amounts's `service user participation of the person`)
          THEN amounts's `of which expenses arising from participation as a service user`
          ELSE 0)

-- src:954 | (4) The following benefits are to be treated as employed earnings—
-- src:955 | (a) statutory sick pay;
-- src:956 | (b) statutory maternity pay;
-- src:957 | (c) ... statutory paternity pay;
-- src:958 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:959 | (e) statutory adoption pay; ...
-- src:960 | (f) statutory shared parental pay; ...
-- src:961 | (g) statutory parental bereavement pay ; and
-- src:962 | (h) statutory neonatal care pay.
@ref reg 55(4) (src:954-962)
GIVEN benefit IS A Benefit
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 55(4) — a benefit treated as employed earnings` benefit MEANS
    CONSIDER benefit
    WHEN `statutory sick pay`                 THEN TRUE
    WHEN `statutory maternity pay`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `statutory paternity pay`            THEN TRUE
    WHEN `statutory adoption pay`             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `statutory shared parental pay`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN `statutory parental bereavement pay` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `statutory neonatal care pay`        THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:954 | (4) The following benefits are to be treated as employed earnings—
-- src:955 | (a) statutory sick pay;
-- src:956 | (b) statutory maternity pay;
-- src:957 | (c) ... statutory paternity pay;
-- src:958 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:959 | (e) statutory adoption pay; ...
-- src:960 | (f) statutory shared parental pay; ...
-- src:961 | (g) statutory parental bereavement pay ; and
-- src:962 | (h) statutory neonatal care pay.
@ref reg 55(4) (src:954-962)
GIVEN amounts IS AN `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 55(4) — the benefits treated as employed earnings` amounts MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN payment YIELD payment's amount)
             (filter (GIVEN payment YIELD `reg 55(4) — a benefit treated as employed earnings` (payment's benefit)) (amounts's `benefits received`)))

-- src:963 | (4A) A repayment of income tax or national insurance contributions received by a person from HMRC in respect of a tax year in which the person was in paid work is to be treated as employed earnings unless it is taken into account as self-employed earnings under regulation 57(4).
@ref reg 55(4A) (src:963)
GIVEN amounts IS AN `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 55(4A) — the repayment treated as employed earnings` amounts MEANS
    IF     (`reg 2 — paid work` (amounts's `work done by the person in that tax year`))
       AND (NOT (amounts's `the repayment is taken into account as self-employed earnings under regulation 57(4)`))
    THEN amounts's `repayment of income tax or national insurance contributions received from HMRC in respect of a tax year`
    ELSE 0

-- src:964 | (5) In calculating the amount of a person's employed earnings in respect of an assessment period, there are to be deducted from the amount of general earnings or benefits specified in paragraphs (2) to (4)—
-- src:965 | (a) any relievable pension contributions made by the person in that period;
-- src:966 | (b) any amounts paid by the person in that period in respect of the employment by way of income tax or primary Class 1 contributions under section 6(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act; and
-- src:967 | (c) any sums withheld as donations to an approved scheme under Part 12 of ITEPA (payroll giving) by a person required to make deductions or repayments of income tax under the PAYE Regulations.
@ref reg 55(5) (src:964-967)
GIVEN amounts IS AN `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 55(5) — the amounts deducted` amounts MEANS
        (amounts's `relievable pension contributions made by the person in the assessment period`)
    PLUS (amounts's `amounts paid by the person in the assessment period in respect of the employment by way of income tax or primary Class 1 contributions`)
    PLUS (amounts's `sums withheld as donations to an approved scheme under Part 12 of ITEPA (payroll giving)`)

-- The result is not floored at nil: the paragraphs state no floor (contrast regulation 57(2), which states one in words). Fork F-E1.
-- src:946 | 55 Employed earnings
-- src:947 | (1) This regulation applies for the purposes of calculating earned income from employment under a contract of service or in an office, including elective office (“employed earnings”).
-- src:948 | (2) Employed earnings comprise any amounts that are general earnings, as defined in section 7(3) of ITEPA, but excluding—
-- src:949 | (a) amounts that are treated as earnings under Chapters 2 to 11 of Part 3 of ITEPA (the benefits code); and
-- src:950 | (b) amounts that are exempt from income tax under Part 4 of ITEPA.
-- src:951 | (3) In the calculation of employed earnings the following are to be disregarded—
-- src:952 | (a) expenses that are allowed to be deducted under Chapter 2 of Part 5 of ITEPA; and
-- src:953 | (b) expenses arising from participation as a service user (see regulation 53(2)).
-- src:954 | (4) The following benefits are to be treated as employed earnings—
-- src:955 | (a) statutory sick pay;
-- src:956 | (b) statutory maternity pay;
-- src:957 | (c) ... statutory paternity pay;
-- src:958 | (d) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:959 | (e) statutory adoption pay; ...
-- src:960 | (f) statutory shared parental pay; ...
-- src:961 | (g) statutory parental bereavement pay ; and
-- src:962 | (h) statutory neonatal care pay.
-- src:963 | (4A) A repayment of income tax or national insurance contributions received by a person from HMRC in respect of a tax year in which the person was in paid work is to be treated as employed earnings unless it is taken into account as self-employed earnings under regulation 57(4).
-- src:964 | (5) In calculating the amount of a person's employed earnings in respect of an assessment period, there are to be deducted from the amount of general earnings or benefits specified in paragraphs (2) to (4)—
-- src:965 | (a) any relievable pension contributions made by the person in that period;
-- src:966 | (b) any amounts paid by the person in that period in respect of the employment by way of income tax or primary Class 1 contributions under section 6(1) of the Contributions and Benefits Act; and
-- src:967 | (c) any sums withheld as donations to an approved scheme under Part 12 of ITEPA (payroll giving) by a person required to make deductions or repayments of income tax under the PAYE Regulations.
@ref reg 55 (src:946-967)
GIVEN amounts IS AN `Amounts received from an employment in an assessment period`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 55 — the employed earnings for an assessment period` amounts MEANS
    `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny`
        (   (`reg 55(2) — the general earnings that comprise employed earnings` amounts)
          MINUS (`reg 55(3) — the amounts disregarded` amounts)
          PLUS (`reg 55(4) — the benefits treated as employed earnings` amounts)
          PLUS (`reg 55(4A) — the repayment treated as employed earnings` amounts)
          MINUS (`reg 55(5) — the amounts deducted` amounts))

§§ `Regulation 56 -- Employee involved in trade dispute`

-- src:968 | 56 Employee involved in trade dispute
-- src:969 | A person who has had employed earnings and has withdrawn their labour in furtherance of a trade dispute is, unless their contract of service has been terminated, to be assumed to have employed earnings at the same level as they would have had were it not for the trade dispute.
@ref reg 56 (src:968-969)
DECLARE `Employee involved in a trade dispute` HAS
    `the person has had employed earnings`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has withdrawn their labour in furtherance of a trade dispute`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's contract of service has been terminated`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `employed earnings the person would have had were it not for the trade dispute`           IS A NUMBER
    `employed earnings the person has`                                                        IS A NUMBER

-- src:968 | 56 Employee involved in trade dispute
-- src:969 | A person who has had employed earnings and has withdrawn their labour in furtherance of a trade dispute is, unless their contract of service has been terminated, to be assumed to have employed earnings at the same level as they would have had were it not for the trade dispute.
@ref reg 56 (src:968-969)
GIVEN employee IS AN `Employee involved in a trade dispute`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 56 — the employed earnings assumed for an employee involved in a trade dispute` employee MEANS
    IF     (employee's `the person has had employed earnings`)
       AND (employee's `the person has withdrawn their labour in furtherance of a trade dispute`)
       AND (NOT (employee's `the person's contract of service has been terminated`))
    THEN employee's `employed earnings the person would have had were it not for the trade dispute`
    ELSE employee's `employed earnings the person has`

§§ `Regulation 60 -- Notional earned income`

-- src:1028 | 60 Notional earned income
-- src:1029 | (1) A person who has deprived themselves of earned income, or whose employer has arranged for them to be so deprived, for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit is to be treated as possessing that earned income.
-- src:1030 | (2) Such a purpose is to be treated as existing if, in fact, entitlement or higher entitlement to universal credit did result and, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, this was a foreseeable and intended consequence of the deprivation.
@ref reg 60(1) and (2) (src:1028-1030)
DECLARE `Deprivation of earned income` HAS
    `amount of the earned income of which the person has been deprived`                       IS A NUMBER
    `the person has deprived themselves of earned income`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's employer has arranged for the person to be deprived of earned income`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the deprivation was for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `entitlement or higher entitlement to universal credit did in fact result`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the opinion of the Secretary of State this was a foreseeable and intended consequence of the deprivation`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1030 | (2) Such a purpose is to be treated as existing if, in fact, entitlement or higher entitlement to universal credit did result and, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, this was a foreseeable and intended consequence of the deprivation.
@ref reg 60(2) (src:1030)
GIVEN deprivation IS A `Deprivation of earned income`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 60(2) — the purpose is treated as existing` deprivation MEANS
        (deprivation's `entitlement or higher entitlement to universal credit did in fact result`)
    AND (deprivation's `in the opinion of the Secretary of State this was a foreseeable and intended consequence of the deprivation`)

-- src:1029 | (1) A person who has deprived themselves of earned income, or whose employer has arranged for them to be so deprived, for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit is to be treated as possessing that earned income.
@ref reg 60(1) (src:1029)
GIVEN deprivation IS A `Deprivation of earned income`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 60(1) — the person has been deprived of earned income` deprivation MEANS
        (deprivation's `the person has deprived themselves of earned income`)
    OR  (deprivation's `the person's employer has arranged for the person to be deprived of earned income`)

-- src:1029 | (1) A person who has deprived themselves of earned income, or whose employer has arranged for them to be so deprived, for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit is to be treated as possessing that earned income.
@ref reg 60(1) (src:1029)
GIVEN deprivation IS A `Deprivation of earned income`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 60(1) — the purpose existed` deprivation MEANS
        (deprivation's `the deprivation was for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit`)
    OR  (`reg 60(2) — the purpose is treated as existing` deprivation)

-- src:1029 | (1) A person who has deprived themselves of earned income, or whose employer has arranged for them to be so deprived, for the purpose of securing entitlement to universal credit or to an increased amount of universal credit is to be treated as possessing that earned income.
@ref reg 60(1) (src:1029)
GIVEN deprivation IS A `Deprivation of earned income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 60(1) — the earned income the person is treated as possessing` deprivation MEANS
    IF     (`reg 60(1) — the person has been deprived of earned income` deprivation)
       AND (`reg 60(1) — the purpose existed` deprivation)
    THEN deprivation's `amount of the earned income of which the person has been deprived`
    ELSE 0

-- src:1031 | (3) If a person provides services for another person and—
-- src:1032 | (a) the other person makes no payment for those services or pays less than would be paid for comparable services in the same location; and
-- src:1033 | (b) the means of the other person were sufficient to pay for, or pay more for, those services,
-- src:1034 | the person who provides the services is to be treated as having received the remuneration that would be reasonable for the provision of those services.
@ref reg 60(3) (src:1031-1034)
DECLARE `Services provided by a person for another person` HAS
    `payment the other person makes for those services`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `amount that would be paid for comparable services in the same location`                  IS A NUMBER
    `the means of the other person were sufficient to pay for, or pay more for, those services`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `remuneration that would be reasonable for the provision of those services`              IS A NUMBER

-- src:1035 | (4) Paragraph (3) does not apply where—
-- src:1036 | (a) the person is engaged to provide the services by a charitable or voluntary organisation and the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is reasonable to provide the services free of charge or at less than the rate that would be paid for comparable services in the same location;
-- src:1037 | (b) the services are provided by a person who is participating as a service user (see regulation 53(2)); or
-- src:1038 | (c) the services are provided under or in connection with a person's participation in an employment or training programme approved by the Secretary of State.
@ref reg 60(4) (src:1035-1038)
DECLARE `Services to which regulation 60(3) may not apply` HAS
    `the person is engaged to provide the services by a charitable or voluntary organisation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is reasonable to provide the services free of charge or at less than the rate that would be paid for comparable services in the same location`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `service user participation of the person`                                                IS A `Person who may be participating as a service user`
    `the services are provided under or in connection with a person's participation in an employment or training programme approved by the Secretary of State`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:1036 | (a) the person is engaged to provide the services by a charitable or voluntary organisation and the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is reasonable to provide the services free of charge or at less than the rate that would be paid for comparable services in the same location;
@ref reg 60(4)(a) (src:1036)
GIVEN services IS A `Services to which regulation 60(3) may not apply`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 60(4)(a) — engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation and it is reasonable that the services are free or cheap` services MEANS
        (services's `the person is engaged to provide the services by a charitable or voluntary organisation`)
    AND (services's `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is reasonable to provide the services free of charge or at less than the rate that would be paid for comparable services in the same location`)

-- src:1035 | (4) Paragraph (3) does not apply where—
-- src:1036 | (a) the person is engaged to provide the services by a charitable or voluntary organisation and the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is reasonable to provide the services free of charge or at less than the rate that would be paid for comparable services in the same location;
-- src:1037 | (b) the services are provided by a person who is participating as a service user (see regulation 53(2)); or
-- src:1038 | (c) the services are provided under or in connection with a person's participation in an employment or training programme approved by the Secretary of State.
@ref reg 60(4) (src:1035-1038)
GIVEN services IS A `Services to which regulation 60(3) may not apply`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 60(4) — paragraph (3) does not apply` services MEANS
        (`reg 60(4)(a) — engaged by a charitable or voluntary organisation and it is reasonable that the services are free or cheap` services)
    OR  (`reg 53(2) — the person is participating as a service user` (services's `service user participation of the person`))
    OR  (services's `the services are provided under or in connection with a person's participation in an employment or training programme approved by the Secretary of State`)

-- src:1032 | (a) the other person makes no payment for those services or pays less than would be paid for comparable services in the same location; and
-- src:1033 | (b) the means of the other person were sufficient to pay for, or pay more for, those services,
@ref reg 60(3)(a) and (b) (src:1032-1033)
GIVEN services IS A `Services provided by a person for another person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 60(3) — the other person pays nothing or less than would be paid for comparable services and could have paid more` services MEANS
        (    (services's `payment the other person makes for those services` EQUALS 0)
         OR  (services's `payment the other person makes for those services` LESS THAN services's `amount that would be paid for comparable services in the same location`))
    AND (services's `the means of the other person were sufficient to pay for, or pay more for, those services`)

-- src:1031 | (3) If a person provides services for another person and—
-- src:1032 | (a) the other person makes no payment for those services or pays less than would be paid for comparable services in the same location; and
-- src:1033 | (b) the means of the other person were sufficient to pay for, or pay more for, those services,
-- src:1034 | the person who provides the services is to be treated as having received the remuneration that would be reasonable for the provision of those services.
@ref reg 60(3) (src:1031-1034)
GIVEN services IS A `Services provided by a person for another person`
      exceptions IS A `Services to which regulation 60(3) may not apply`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`reg 60(3) — the remuneration the person is treated as having received` services exceptions MEANS
    IF     (`reg 60(3) — the other person pays nothing or less than would be paid for comparable services and could have paid more` services)
       AND (NOT (`reg 60(4) — paragraph (3) does not apply` exceptions))
    THEN JUST (`core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (services's `remuneration that would be reasonable for the provision of those services`))
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Regulation 61 -- Information for calculating earned income: real time information etc.`

-- Paragraph (1): unless paragraph (2) applies, a person must provide the information the Secretary of State requires, at the times
-- the Secretary of State requires it. Paragraph (2) applies where the employer is a Real Time Information employer (defined in
-- regulation 2A(1) of the PAYE Regulations, a pure citation: a stated fact).
-- src:1039 | 61 Information for calculating earned income – real time information etc.
-- src:1040 | (1) Unless paragraph (2) applies, a person must provide such information for the purposes of calculating their earned income at such times as the Secretary of State may require.
@ref reg 61(1) (src:1039-1040)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State requires the information at that time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earned income is from an employment whose employer is a Real Time Information employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 61(1) — the person must provide the information for calculating their earned income` `the Secretary of State requires the information at that time` `the earned income is from an employment whose employer is a Real Time Information employer` MEANS
        `the Secretary of State requires the information at that time`
    AND (NOT `the earned income is from an employment whose employer is a Real Time Information employer`)

-- src:1046 | (3) Paragraph (2) does not apply where—
-- src:1047 | (a) in relation to a particular employment the Secretary of State considers that the employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner;
-- src:1048 | (b) it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in regulation 55 (employed earnings), in some material respect; or
-- src:1049 | (c) no information is received from HMRC in an assessment period and the Secretary of State considers that this is likely to be because of a failure to report information (which includes the failure of a computer system operated by HMRC, the employer or any other person).
@ref reg 61(3) (src:1046-1049)
DECLARE `Employment considered under regulation 61` HAS
    `the employer is a Real Time Information employer`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State considers that the employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in regulation 55 in some material respect`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `no information is received from HMRC in the assessment period and the Secretary of State considers that this is likely to be because of a failure to report information`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount of employed earnings from the employment based on the information reported to HMRC and received by the Secretary of State from HMRC in the assessment period`  IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `amount of employed earnings from the employment determined in accordance with regulation 55`  IS A NUMBER

-- src:1046 | (3) Paragraph (2) does not apply where—
-- src:1047 | (a) in relation to a particular employment the Secretary of State considers that the employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner;
-- src:1048 | (b) it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in regulation 55 (employed earnings), in some material respect; or
-- src:1049 | (c) no information is received from HMRC in an assessment period and the Secretary of State considers that this is likely to be because of a failure to report information (which includes the failure of a computer system operated by HMRC, the employer or any other person).
@ref reg 61(3) (src:1046-1049)
GIVEN employment IS AN `Employment considered under regulation 61`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 61(3) — an exception to the use of Real Time Information applies` employment MEANS
        (employment's `the Secretary of State considers that the employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner`)
    OR  (employment's `it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in regulation 55 in some material respect`)
    OR  (employment's `no information is received from HMRC in the assessment period and the Secretary of State considers that this is likely to be because of a failure to report information`)

-- src:1042 | (2) Where a person is, or has been, engaged in an employment in respect of which their employer is a Real Time Information employer—
-- src:1043 | (a) the amount of the person’s employed earnings from that employment in respect of each assessment period is to be based on the information reported to HMRC under the PAYE Regulations and received by the Secretary of State from HMRC in that assessment period; and
-- src:1044 | (b) in respect of an assessment period in which no information is received from HMRC, the amount of employed earnings in relation to that employment is to be taken to be nil.
@ref reg 61(2) (src:1042-1044)
GIVEN employment IS AN `Employment considered under regulation 61`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 61(2) — the employed earnings are based on Real Time Information` employment MEANS
        (employment's `the employer is a Real Time Information employer`)
    AND (NOT (`reg 61(3) — an exception to the use of Real Time Information applies` employment))

-- Paragraphs (2) and (4): the employed earnings for the assessment period are the information received from HMRC in that period
-- (nil if none was received), unless an exception in (3) applies, in which case the Secretary of State determines them under
-- regulation 55 using such information or evidence as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
-- src:1042 | (2) Where a person is, or has been, engaged in an employment in respect of which their employer is a Real Time Information employer—
-- src:1043 | (a) the amount of the person’s employed earnings from that employment in respect of each assessment period is to be based on the information reported to HMRC under the PAYE Regulations and received by the Secretary of State from HMRC in that assessment period; and
-- src:1044 | (b) in respect of an assessment period in which no information is received from HMRC, the amount of employed earnings in relation to that employment is to be taken to be nil.
-- src:1045 | Exceptions to use of Real Time Information
-- src:1046 | (3) Paragraph (2) does not apply where—
-- src:1047 | (a) in relation to a particular employment the Secretary of State considers that the employer is unlikely to report information to HMRC in a sufficiently accurate or timely manner;
-- src:1048 | (b) it appears to the Secretary of State that the amount of a payment reported to HMRC is incorrect, or fails to reflect the definition of employed earnings in regulation 55 (employed earnings), in some material respect; or
-- src:1049 | (c) no information is received from HMRC in an assessment period and the Secretary of State considers that this is likely to be because of a failure to report information (which includes the failure of a computer system operated by HMRC, the employer or any other person).
-- src:1050 | (4) Where paragraph (2) does not apply by virtue of any of the exceptions in paragraph (3) the Sectary of State must determine the amount of employed earnings for the assessment period in question (or, where the exception in paragraph (3)(a) applies, for each assessment period in which the person is engaged in that employment) in accordance with regulation 55 (employed earning) using such information or evidence as the Secretary of State thinks fit.
@ref reg 61(2) and (4) (src:1042-1050)
GIVEN employment IS AN `Employment considered under regulation 61`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 61(2) and (4) — the employed earnings from the employment for an assessment period` employment MEANS
    IF `reg 61(2) — the employed earnings are based on Real Time Information` employment
    THEN (CONSIDER employment's `amount of employed earnings from the employment based on the information reported to HMRC and received by the Secretary of State from HMRC in the assessment period`
          WHEN JUST reported THEN reported
          WHEN NOTHING THEN 0)
    ELSE employment's `amount of employed earnings from the employment determined in accordance with regulation 55`

-- src:1051 | Reallocation of reported payments
-- src:1052 | (5) Where it appears to the Secretary of State that a payment of employed earnings has been reported late, or otherwise reported in the wrong assessment period, the Secretary of State may determine that the payment is to be treated as employed earnings in the assessment period in which it was received.
@ref reg 61(5) (src:1051-1052)
DECLARE `Payment of employed earnings that may have been reported late` HAS
    `the payment has been reported late, or otherwise reported in the wrong assessment period`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State determines that the payment is to be treated as employed earnings in the assessment period in which it was received`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `assessment period in which the payment was reported`                                      IS AN `Assessment period`
    `assessment period in which the payment was received`                                      IS AN `Assessment period`

-- src:1051 | Reallocation of reported payments
-- src:1052 | (5) Where it appears to the Secretary of State that a payment of employed earnings has been reported late, or otherwise reported in the wrong assessment period, the Secretary of State may determine that the payment is to be treated as employed earnings in the assessment period in which it was received.
@ref reg 61(5) (src:1051-1052)
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment of employed earnings that may have been reported late`
GIVETH AN `Assessment period`
`reg 61(5) — the assessment period in which the payment is treated as employed earnings` payment MEANS
    IF     (payment's `the payment has been reported late, or otherwise reported in the wrong assessment period`)
       AND (payment's `the Secretary of State determines that the payment is to be treated as employed earnings in the assessment period in which it was received`)
    THEN payment's `assessment period in which the payment was received`
    ELSE payment's `assessment period in which the payment was reported`

-- src:1053 | (6) Where a person is engaged in an employment where they are paid on a regular monthly basis and more than one payment in relation to that employment is reported in the same assessment period, the Secretary of State may, for the purposes of maintaining a regular pattern, determine that one of those payments is to be treated as employed earnings in respect of a different assessment period.
@ref reg 61(6) (src:1053)
DECLARE `Regular monthly payment that may be moved to a different assessment period` HAS
    `the person is engaged in an employment where they are paid on a regular monthly basis`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `more than one payment in relation to that employment is reported in the same assessment period`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Secretary of State determines, for the purposes of maintaining a regular pattern, that one of those payments is to be treated as employed earnings in respect of a different assessment period`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `assessment period in which the payment was reported`                                      IS AN `Assessment period`
    `the different assessment period`                                                         IS A MAYBE `Assessment period`

-- src:1053 | (6) Where a person is engaged in an employment where they are paid on a regular monthly basis and more than one payment in relation to that employment is reported in the same assessment period, the Secretary of State may, for the purposes of maintaining a regular pattern, determine that one of those payments is to be treated as employed earnings in respect of a different assessment period.
@ref reg 61(6) (src:1053)
GIVEN payment IS A `Regular monthly payment that may be moved to a different assessment period`
GIVETH AN `Assessment period`
`reg 61(6) — the assessment period in which one of the payments is treated as employed earnings` payment MEANS
    IF     (payment's `the person is engaged in an employment where they are paid on a regular monthly basis`)
       AND (payment's `more than one payment in relation to that employment is reported in the same assessment period`)
       AND (payment's `the Secretary of State determines, for the purposes of maintaining a regular pattern, that one of those payments is to be treated as employed earnings in respect of a different assessment period`)
    THEN (CONSIDER payment's `the different assessment period`
          WHEN JUST different THEN different
          WHEN NOTHING THEN payment's `assessment period in which the payment was reported`)
    ELSE payment's `assessment period in which the payment was reported`

-- Paragraph (7): where the Secretary of State has made a determination under (4), (5) or (6), the Secretary of State may make
-- such other adjustments as are necessary to avoid duplication or to maintain a regular payment pattern. The adjustment is the
-- Secretary of State's, so it is a plain input.
-- src:1054 | Consequential adjustments
-- src:1055 | (7) Where the Secretary of State makes a determination under any of paragraphs (4) to (6), the Secretary of State may make such other adjustments to the calculation of the person’s employed earnings as may be necessary to avoid duplication or to maintain a regular payment pattern.
@ref reg 61(7) (src:1054-1055)
GIVEN `employed earnings before any adjustment` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary of State has made a determination under paragraph (4), (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `adjustment the Secretary of State makes as necessary to avoid duplication or to maintain a regular payment pattern` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 61(7) — the employed earnings after any consequential adjustment` `employed earnings before any adjustment` `the Secretary of State has made a determination under paragraph (4), (5) or (6)` `adjustment the Secretary of State makes as necessary to avoid duplication or to maintain a regular payment pattern` MEANS
    IF `the Secretary of State has made a determination under paragraph (4), (5) or (6)`
    THEN `core — an amount rounded to the nearest penny` (`employed earnings before any adjustment` PLUS `adjustment the Secretary of State makes as necessary to avoid duplication or to maintain a regular payment pattern`)
    ELSE `employed earnings before any adjustment`

§§ `Regulation 61(8) -- Definition of "Real Time Information Employer" (inert)`
-- src:1056 | (8) In this regulation “Real Time Information Employer” has the meaning in regulation 2A(1) of the PAYE Regulations.
-- INERT: defines "Real Time Information Employer" by pure citation of regulation 2A(1) of the PAYE Regulations, which is not an
-- input. The fact is the field `the employer is a Real Time Information employer` of `Employment considered under regulation 61`.
